These are the profile values. Home Assistant scales them to every cover that follows it, in proportion to that cover's curtain travel.

{values}
Covers following it: {followers}

calibration_actions.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

What is kept for this cover:

{values}
**Where its values come from**: {origin}.

**What you have to do**: choose what to do with it. “Measure it again” runs the guided calibration on this cover and replaces what is here; “Delete the calibration” hands this cover back to the configuration file, if you use one, to the profile it follows, or to the defaults.

calibration_delete.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

**What is about to happen**: the values kept for this cover are removed and the cover goes back to what the configuration file says, if you use one, or to the profile it follows.

The measurements cannot be recovered: getting them back means running the guided calibration again.

home_closed_done.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

**What happened**: the cover was closed completely: this way everything measured from here on starts from a known point.

**What you have to do**: look at it. If it is completely closed, slats shut and the bottom edge resting, go on. If it is still moving, wait and then go on. If it did not move at all, or moved the wrong way, say so below.

open_lift.description:
![](/myhome_static/lift_off.webp)

**Cover**: {cover}

Press as soon as the bottom edge leaves the base.

lift_early.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

**What happened**: a gap of less than a centimetre means the cover was still resting on its base when the motor stopped, so the press was made before the bottom edge left it. The slat opening time it measured is short by an unknown amount, and no reading can put back a distance that was never travelled.

**What you have to do**: make the ascent again. The cover is sent back down and starts up once more; this time wait until the bottom edge has really lifted before pressing.

closed_again.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

**What happened**: the cover was sent back down to the base, because the full ascent has to start from there exactly as the first run did.

**What you have to do**: look at it. If it is completely closed, slats shut and the bottom edge resting, go on. If it is still moving, wait and then go on. If it did not move at all, or moved the wrong way, say so below.

open_top.description:
![](/myhome_static/top_stop.webp)

**Cover**: {cover}

Press at the instant the motor stops at the top.

open_result.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

**What was measured**: slats {slat} s, full ascent {run} s.

**What you have to do**: if both presses felt right, go on. If either was late or early, repeat the measurement: both runs of the ascent are made again from the base, because a slat opening time taken on one attempt does not belong with an ascent taken on another. A press half a second out moves the estimate by a few centimetres.

close_result.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

**What was measured**: full descent {run} s.

**What you have to do**: if the press felt right, go on. Otherwise repeat the measurement: the cover is sent back up and the descent is run again.

height_result.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

**What was written down**: {height} cm from the base to the bottom edge with the cover completely open.

**What you have to do**: if that is the number you read off the tape, go on. Check the value: the tape readings of the next steps are compared against this curtain travel. If the cover is not completely open, so that this is not the whole travel, say so below: it is opened again and the reading is taken again.

tape_brief.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

**What is about to happen**: from here on the cover moves by itself. Readings to take: {readings}. Each one begins by taking the cover to the end stop that reading is taken from, and where there is a run to measure the cover makes it and stops there on its own. There is nothing to press and nothing to catch in time: after each movement a screen asks for the distance in centimetres.

**What you have to do**: make sure nothing is in the way, keep the tape measure to hand and stand clear while the cover is moving. If a movement does not do what it should, say so on the screen that follows the reading: the step is made again.

verify_offer.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

The curtain travel was all that was needed: the calibration can be saved as it is.

**What the check is**: the cover is sent half way and you measure where it really stopped, which says whether this cover really behaves like the profile. It takes about a minute and one tape reading.

summary_basic.description:
**Cover**: {cover}

**Curtain travel**: {height}

**Where these values go**: if you save, they stay inside Home Assistant, here under Configure → Calibrations. They are written the moment you save, and the cover starts using them when this dialog is closed, instead of the ones in the configuration file, if you use one. From that same screen you can look at them again, correct them by hand or delete them at any time.

If you would rather write them into the file yourself, the equivalent snippet is below: copy it before you close this, because without saving nothing is kept.

{yaml}
The accuracy has not been checked yet. “Continue with the thorough calibration” fits four more points, at a quarter and three quarters of the travel in each direction, and then puts the model to a fifth reading taken where nothing was fitted.

**What you have to do**: save, or continue with five more tape readings, taking about two minutes.

